---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '~/components/Section.astro';
import ImpactStats from '~/components/ImpactStats.astro';

/**
 * HOME PAGE.
 *
 * The hero is the decided tagline — "Food is a human right." — set alone, with
 * no trailing qualifier. It is a belief statement, so the lead paragraph
 * underneath it does the work of saying who we are and what we actually do.
 *
 * Positioning this page has to hold, in this order:
 *   1. Share Meals is a nonprofit dedicated to food security. Not "an app".
 *      Technology is one of the tools; it is never the headline.
 *   2. Colleges are the roots and still the main service population, but they
 *      are credibility, not scope — campus appears in body copy and never in
 *      the tagline or an H1, so the brand is not siloed to it.
 *   3. Non-tech direct service is a side note, mentioned once, not a section.
 *
 * Copy follows the dignity-first language rule: food that is shared is food,
 * and the mission is framed as ensuring food security rather than against
 * insecurity.
 *
 * The closing band of figures comes from the backend at runtime and disappears
 * entirely if the numbers cannot be fetched — see ImpactStats.astro. Nothing
 * on this page should be written to depend on it being there.
 *
 * There are no call-to-action buttons because there are no pages to point them
 * at yet. A button that goes nowhere is worse than no button.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Share Meals — food is a human right"
  description="Share Meals is a nonprofit dedicated to food security. Some of that work is software. Some of it is showing up with food."
  bareTitle
>
  <Section size="hero">
    <h1 class="text-display-2xl font-extrabold text-balance m-0">
      Food is a<br />
      <span class="text-[var(--color-brand-700)]">human right.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="text-lead mt-8 max-w-2xl text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
      Share Meals is a nonprofit dedicated to food security. Some of that work
      is software. Some of it is showing up with food.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="inverse">
    <h2 class="text-display font-extrabold text-balance m-0">
      Believing it is the easy part.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-lead mt-6 max-w-2xl">
      A right that exists on paper is not a meal in anyone's hands. Closing that
      distance is the whole of our work: software that shows people the food
      already around them, and programs that put food where software alone
      won't reach.
    </p>
    <p class="text-lead mt-6 max-w-2xl">
      We began with college students, and campuses are still where most of our
      work happens. They are not where it stops. A right that only holds on
      campus was never a right.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <ImpactStats />
</BaseLayout>
